namespace Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup

open NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal

/-- The principal ray `P(𝔪)` is contained in the group `I(𝔪)` of fractional ideals coprime to `𝔪`:
a generator of `P(𝔪)` is a principal ideal `(a)` with `a ≡ 1 mod* 𝔪`, and such an `a` is a local
unit at every prime `𝔭 | 𝔪`, so `(a)` has no prime factor dividing `𝔪`
(`fracCoprimeId_spanUnit`), whence it lies in `I(𝔪)` (`mem_idealCoprimeGroupId_iff`). -/
theorem principalRayId_le_idealCoprimeGroupId
    {K : Type} [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔪 : Ideal (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)) (h𝔪 : 𝔪 ≠ ⊥) :
    NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRayId 𝔪 ≤
      NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.idealCoprimeGroupId 𝔪 := by
  rw [NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRayId, Subgroup.closure_le]
  rintro A ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
  exact (Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup.ArtinReciprocity.IdealModulus.mem_idealCoprimeGroupId_iff
      𝔪 _).mpr
    (Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup.ArtinReciprocity.IdealModulus.fracCoprimeId_spanUnit 𝔪 h𝔪 ha)

/-- The norm group `𝔑(𝔪)` is contained in the group `I(𝔪)` of fractional ideals coprime to `𝔪`: a
generator of `𝔑(𝔪)` is the relative norm of an ideal `I` of `L` coprime to `𝔪·𝓞 L`; every prime
`𝔓 | 𝔪·𝓞 L` lies above a prime `𝔭 | 𝔪`, so `v_𝔓(I) = 0` and hence
`v_𝔭(N_{L/K} I) = Σ_{𝔓|𝔭} f(𝔓/𝔭)·v_𝔓(I) = 0` (`fracCoprimeId_relNorm`), giving
`N_{L/K} I ∈ I(𝔪)` (`mem_idealCoprimeGroupId_iff`). -/
theorem normRayId_le_idealCoprimeGroupId
    {K L : Type} [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L] [NumberField L] [Algebra K L]
    [FiniteDimensional K L]
    (𝔪 : Ideal (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)) :
    NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRayId (K := K) (L := L) 𝔪 ≤
      NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.idealCoprimeGroupId 𝔪 := by
  rw [NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRayId, Subgroup.closure_le]
  rintro A ⟨I, hI, hcop, rfl⟩
  exact (Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup.ArtinReciprocity.IdealModulus.mem_idealCoprimeGroupId_iff
      𝔪 _).mpr
    (Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup.ArtinReciprocity.IdealModulus.fracCoprimeId_relNorm 𝔪 hI hcop)

/-- **The principal ray and the norm group of an ideal modulus are coprime to it.**

For `𝔪 : Ideal (𝓞 K)` with `𝔪 ≠ ⊥` and a finite extension `L/K` of number fields:
`P(𝔪) ⊔ 𝔑(𝔪) ≤ I(𝔪)`, i.e. every congruence-`1` principal ideal and every relative norm lies in
the group of fractional ideals coprime to `𝔪`.  This is the companion containment of Lang's index
inequality and the first conjunct of the ideal-modulus `langCyclicRelIndexId`.

For the principal ray: if `a : Kˣ` satisfies `CongrOneId 𝔪 a` then, at `𝔭 | 𝔪` (i.e. `count K 𝔭 𝔪 ≥ 1`,
which is where `h𝔪` is used), the congruence `v (a - 1) ≤ exp (-(count))` forces `ord_𝔭 a = 0`, so
`(a)` is coprime to `𝔪`; since `principalRayId 𝔪` is the closure of the `spanUnit a`
(`CoreId.lean`: `principalRayClId_eq_principalRayId`) this gives the principal half.  For the norm
ray: `normRayId 𝔪` is generated by the norms of ideals of `L` coprime to `𝔪·𝓞 L`; if `𝔭 | 𝔪` then
`𝔪𝓞_L ≤ 𝔮` for every `𝔮 | 𝔭` in `𝓞 L`, so such an ideal has `ord_𝔮 = 0` and hence
`ord_𝔭(relNorm I) = Σ_{𝔮|𝔭} f(𝔮/𝔭)·ord_𝔮(I) = 0`. -/
theorem IdealModulusContainmentProved
    {K L : Type} [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L] [NumberField L] [Algebra K L]
    [FiniteDimensional K L]
    (𝔪 : Ideal (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)) (h𝔪 : 𝔪 ≠ ⊥) :
    (NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRayId 𝔪 ⊔
      NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRayId (K := K) (L := L) 𝔪) ≤
      NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.idealCoprimeGroupId 𝔪 :=
  sup_le (principalRayId_le_idealCoprimeGroupId 𝔪 h𝔪)
    (normRayId_le_idealCoprimeGroupId (K := K) (L := L) 𝔪)

end Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup
